\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Fields with a supplied internal action}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let #{F} be a finite-dimensional #{k}-representation of #{G} as in
the [translation blocks](fdip-016C). On fields #{f:\Lambda\to F} take
#{(T_x f)(y)=f(y+x)} and #{(b f)(y)=b(f(b^{-1}y))}.
Then #{b T_x b^{-1}=T_{b x}} by substitution, giving an action of
#{G_\Lambda}. The fields in block #{r} are exactly
#{f(y)=\alpha_r(y)v} with #{v\in F}. The translation equation at
zero gives this value at every #{y}, and the character multiplication
rule gives the converse. Acting by #{b} sends this field to
#{y\mapsto\alpha_{br}(y)b v}. In particular the action on a single
block by #{G_r} is its given action on #{F} restricted to #{G_r}.}

\p{For a linear character of a normal subgroup,
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.conjNormalFDRep_ofLinearCharacter} gives
the transported character by precomposing with inverse conjugation.
For translations in #{G_\Lambda} this sends #{\alpha_r} to
#{\alpha_r\circ b^{-1}}.}
